feat(run): --dry-run prints the hybrid QEMU+vsim commands; tutorial demo

`andesim run --mode hybrid --dry-run` assembles both legs (the QEMU fast leg
with its staged -readconfig, then the vsim accurate leg) and prints them
shell-quoted instead of spawning -- a faithful preview of exactly what runs.

- render_argv / shell_quote (argv.hpp): POSIX-quoted, copy-pasteable command
  lines (safe tokens pass through; spaces/quotes/empties get single-quoted).
- PlanResult.argvs + PlanOptions.dry_run: run_plan records the fully resolved
  per-leg argvs (placeholders, staged qemu_cfg, threaded state paths) and skips
  the spawn loop; cmd_run prints the labeled commands and returns 0.
- docs: config_gating_tutorial.ipynb gains a live --print-qemu-config + --dry-run
  demo and drops the stale "not yet wired" framing; USER_GUIDE --dry-run note;
  qemu_match_ROADMAP FA3.

Tested: render_argv unit test (plan_test.cpp) + a dry-run acceptance check in
tests/andes_sim/test_andes_sim_print_qemu_config.sh (asserts both legs +
-readconfig). Behavioral change.

